    "requirement": "Within object-member unpacking, a format expecting an array must be reachable with a wrong-type member so the supported array diagnostic can include that member's key.",
    "target_route": "A finite input consisting of a selector byte followed by {\"data\":42} parses as an object. A member-array format would make unpack_object look up data, pass its key to unpack, and dispatch '[' to unpack_array's wrong-type guard.",
    "failure_condition": "The old entry instead calls \"{s?o}\" for object members; o accepts the integer. Its only array format, \"[o!]\", is called only when the root is already an array, and top-level unpack starts with a null parent key. The entry also calls json_unpack without an error object, so it cannot expose diagnostic text.",
